    {
      "session_number": 3,
      "date": "20/09/2026",
      "title": "Unmasked Gods and Blood in the Gardens",
      "recap_text": "",
      "next_session_script": "",
      "episode_synopsis": "Session #3 unveils the dark, hypocritical underpinnings of Dolmak Yar's ruling elite while hurling the party into open conflict. Beneath Via Aurora, Wicander Halovar learns the horrifying truth that his family's 'Candescent Creed' is powered by the harvested blood of Etheon, a chained celestial titan. Disgusted by the revelation and warned by Tyranny that House Halovar has ordered assassinations against their allies, Wicander breaks ranks with his noble bloodline to save Teor Pridesire from a fiendish trap at Mercenat Couturier.\n\nMeanwhile, a violent confrontation erupts at the Watchtower tavern as Thimble, Cadogan, and Octus are ambushed by the Crow Keepers guild. The battle turns instantly when Vaelas shatters the tavern window, striking down the guildmaster Solomon with a blackened Guiding Bolt. Interrogating the surviving rogues, the party discovers that Casimir betrayed Thiazi's rebellion, sold the stolen Stone of Nightsong for a fortune in gold, and fled north to a stronghold in Gormelay alongside Teor's rogue brother, Sid Pridesire.\n\nAs the scattered companions reunite at Halendiel's study, they forge an alliance of outcasts. Hal passes his brother Thiazi's Loy-forged scimitar to the party as Cadogan, Thimble, Teor, Wicander, and Tyranny ride out under the cover of night toward Timon. However, the episode concludes on a catastrophic cliffhanger at Palazzo DeVino: an invisible Taconis assassin brutally executes General Raymond DeVino, and Octus's undead brother Thrand unseals the Stone of Nightsong to purge the room.",
      "chronicle_text": "### Act I: Shadows over Via Aurora and the Watchtower\n\n### Scene 1: The Chained Titan beneath Via Aurora\nIn the subterranean vault beneath Via Aurora, Wicander 'Wiki' Halovar and Tyranny stood before the unsealed Prismatic Return. Inside, a chained celestial titan—Etheon, Wicander's true grandfather—struggled against massive iron shackles. Matriarch Fothark Vanessa Halovar coldly revealed that the 'Candescent Creator' light worshipped by the populace was merely filament extracted from Etheon's blood. Goddard Halovar sprouted luminous feathered wings from his back as he channeled the titan's essence. Vanessa instructed Wicander to abandon true faith and accept his political marriage to Ibeka Dantonio to consolidate power over the city's trade. Retiring to Wicander's private bathhouse, Tyranny admitted that while she was contracted to his family, she respected Wicander's genuine conviction and warned him that Fothark Vanessa had already dispatched assassins disguised as tailors at Mercenat Couturier to eliminate Teor Pridesire.\n\n### Scene 2: Confrontation at the Pentevral\nAt the Pentevral Transmutation School, Murray Magneson witnessed Lord Primus Taconis aggressively confronting former Dean Elipides 'Tall Barrel', demanding the immediate surrender of his rogue son, Octus Taconis. When Murray tried to defuse the situation with sarcastic banter, Lord Primus targeted her with a chilling gaze, forcing Murray to succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (rolling a 21) to resist a paralyzing curse. Murray attempted to cast Detect Magic surreptitiously (Deception check 14), but Dean Elipides deliberately knocked over a kettle, counterspelling the magic to shield her before resigning his post. Recognizing the noble families were purging the academy, Murray rushed out to find Captain Azune Nayar in Caravan Hill.\n\n### Scene 3: The Ambush at the Watchtower Tavern\nInside the Watchtower tavern, Thimble, Octus, and Cadogan Vale (accompanied by his hound Wulfric) were cornered by Solomon, a Crow Keepers guildmaster, and several armed rogues wielding burlap sacks. Thimble initiated combat on initiative 25, attempting to intimidate a thug before ducking into his trousers (Stealth 14). Octus cast Cause Fear on Solomon, who succeeded his Wisdom save with a 19. Cadogan attempted an unarmed grapple, rolling an 8 and tripping over a kettle. Three rogues bound Wulfric (Athletics check success) and dealt 7 damage to Cadogan. Suddenly, Vaelas crashed through the tavern window, executing a flawless flanking maneuver with her spiked sensor-whip—rolling a Natural 20 for 13 damage and instantly slaying the lead thug. Thimble illuminated Solomon with Faerie Fire, allowing Octus to strike him with a Fire Bolt (17 to hit, 3 fire damage) and Cadogan to deal 9 bludgeoning damage with his macabre flail. Vaelas sealed Solomon's fate with a blackened Guiding Bolt combined with Hunter's Mark for 18 radiant damage, dropping the guildmaster dead. Vaelas then bellowed an Intimidation check (rolling a 21), causing the remaining rogues to flee in terror. Interrogating the surviving rogue, Gavri, the party learned that Casimir had paid off his guild debts using gold and a deed to a stronghold in Gormelay (Timon), fleeing the city alongside Sid Pridesire in a stolen tricked carriage after selling the Stone of Nightsong.\n\n### Act II: Rescues, Recollections, and Broken Vows\n\n### Scene 4: Echoes of the Shapers at Rondo of the Alhambra\nHalendiel 'Hal' Fang and Tysha Loy visited the ruined amphitheater 'The Rondo of the Alhambra', where Shadia and Olgud Akarat were preparing an independent theater space for the city's commoners. Tysha communed with the ancient cedar tree at the center of the stage, reflecting on her fear of losing her family and the weight of the city's dark history. Bolaire arrived shortly after in an Arcanum carriage delivering six massive ceramic amphoras of lead-laced illusion-conjurative paint recovered from Thiazi's study. Inspecting the paint (Arcana check 21), Bolaire noticed an unnatural aura of ancient conjuration magic that triggered a sudden, sickening nausea (Constitution save 13).\n\n### Scene 5: The Fiendish Trap at Mercenat Couturier\nTeor Pridesire arrived at Mercenat Couturier under the guise of acquiring official Candescent Creed vestments. The shopkeepers, Calastro and Rullius Mercenat, offered him poisoned sherry infused with fiendish incense. Teor activated Divine Sense to detect fiends, but was forced to roll Wisdom saving throws with disadvantage, failing with a 6 and a Natural 2. Paralyzed, Teor was dragged into the basement and suspended above a nine-point pentagram where fiendish tailors began slicing his shadow into pieces. Moments later, Wicander and Tyranny entered the shop. Using high diplomacy and bluffing (Persuasion check 18), Wicander demanded Teor's immediate release. The tailors reluctantly yielded Teor and his belongings. Wicander cast Lesser Restoration to cleanse the paralysis, and Tyranny warned them both that House Halovar had marked them for death.\n\n### Scene 6: The Rescue and Convergence at Hal's Study\nOutside Hal's home, Sir Julian DeVino intercepted Octus, Vaelas, Cadogan, and Thimble. Julian attempted to seize Thimble by her wings, utilizing his Tactical Mind maneuver (Athletics total 27 vs Thimble's 22) to hold her fast while warning Octus that House Taconis enforcers were actively hunting him. After Julian departed, the entire scattered party coalesced at Hal's study. Piece by piece, the truth emerged: Casimir and Sid Pridesire had stolen the Stone of Nightsong and fled north to Gormelay; House Halovar was funneling titan blood into fake holy water; and House Taconis was aggressively purging anyone connected to Thiazi. Renouncing his family's dark legacy, Wicander offered a sincere apology to the group, while Hal retrieved his brother Thiazi's Loy-forged scimitar from his study wall. The party resolved to leave Dolmak Yar together and travel north to Timon to hunt down Casimir and reclaim the Stone of Nightsong.\n\n### Act III: Blood in the Palazzo\n\n### Scene 7: Gathering of Outcasts and The Flight North\nWhile Cadogan, Thimble, Teor, Wicander, and Tyranny finalized their travel plans and acquired wilderness supplies, Captain Azune Nayar and Murray Magneson arrived at Hal's study. Azune agreed to cover their escape from the city, while Hal recited the names of the fallen fallen rebels from the Falconer's Rebellion to bless their journey. Five companions mounted horses provided by the rebel network and rode through the northern gates toward Gormelay.\n\n### Scene 8: The Assassination of General Raymond DeVino\nSimultaneously, Sir Julian DeVino, Vaelas, and Octus entered Palazzo DeVino to meet with General Raymond DeVino and Lady Eranessa Royce. While walking the palatial gardens, Vaelas activated her Divine Sense, perceiving hundreds of restless specters surrounding the estate grounds. Suddenly, an invisible Taconis enforcer materialized behind General Raymond, ripping his spinal cord out through his neck and killing the military patriarch instantly. Moments later, six ghoul-like Taconis assassins dressed in crimson robes broke into the upper chambers, led by Octus's undead brother, Thrand Taconis. Thrand held up a glowing, pixelated sphere—the recovered Stone of Nightsong—and commanded his ghouls to execute everyone in the room.",
      "closing_expectations": "The party is split across two dramatic fronts: Cadogan, Thimble, Teor, Wicander, and Tyranny are riding north toward Gormelay to track down Casimir and Sid Pridesire, while Sir Julian, Vaelas, and Octus are trapped inside Palazzo DeVino facing an undead Taconis strike team immediately following the brutal assassination of General Raymond DeVino.",
